{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Q-Metal Morphoid","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/q-metal-morphoid.webp","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/q-metal-morphoid.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Q-Metal Morphoid","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":200,"temp":0,"max":200,"details":""},"ac":{"value":36,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"burrow","value":20}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"paralyzed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"sleep","exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"physical","value":10,"exceptions":["adamantine"],"doubleVs":[]},{"type":"fire","value":15,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["aklo","petran"],"details":""},"level":{"value":14},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Q-metal morphoids are metal elementals made of the strange and extremely rare special material known as q-metal, a silvery metal that bursts into flames when struck. Morphoids appear to somehow be both the avatars and creators of the metal at the same time; q-metal deposits are always found with a morphoid as a guardian, and the deposits grow as the morphoid extends their territory. This leads to an interesting chicken-and-egg question, though whichever came first, they seem to have originated from fallen meteoroids. Q-metal morphoids are able to create multiple appendages that detach from their bodies, and some enterprising individuals have attempted to taunt morphoids into throwing their appendages at them in order to collect the material and run away. This strategy is not recommended for anyone who doesn't desire a fiery death.</p>\n<h2>Q Is For Questions</h2>\n<p>Q-metal has a number of potential applications, from more efficient smithing to flaming ammunition, but no research institution has obtained a large enough sample to perform a comprehensive analysis of its properties. Is the metal actually alive, and is there a hivemind that controls the morphoids? How do existing deposits expand without new meteoroids introducing more of the metal to the earth? Are the metal's properties magical or alchemical in nature? Unfortunately, only goblins have been reckless enough to obtain q-metal in any notable quantity, and they always end up wasting it to start forest fires.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 560/1,250/2,300 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing, slashing), armor (heavy), shield, perception item, skill items (Athletics, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, dexterity, elongating, energy resistant (fire, positive), fire, strength, throwing, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Elizabeth Heyeck","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":8},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":8},"int":{"mod":4},"wis":{"mod":5},"cha":{"mod":-4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":25,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":90}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":28,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":28},"stealth":{"base":23}},"traits":{"value":["elemental"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"lg"}}},"img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/Portraits/q-metal-morphoid.webp","items":[{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"Darkvision","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Darkvision]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"darkvision","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Bestiary","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"type":"action","flags":{"core":{}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1689023872968,"modifiedTime":1689023872968,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.qCCLZhnp2HhP3Ex6","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"_id":"CZ1ajFjLdPjjRZXi"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"Tremorsense (Imprecise) 90 feet","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Tremorsense]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"tremorsense","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Bestiary","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"type":"action","flags":{"core":{}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1689023876991,"modifiedTime":1689023886709,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.j2wsK6IsW5yMW1jW","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"_id":"M1ATS2mJ7m1Ver3i"},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Flame Shroud","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The q-metal morphoid is exposed to fire</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The exterior of the morphoid's body is covered in flames for [[/br 1d4 #Rounds]]{1d4 rounds}. This adds 1d6 fire damage to the morphoid's melee unarmed attacks. Additionally, adjacent creatures that hit the morphoid with a melee attack, as well as creatures that touch the morphoid or hit the morphoid with an unarmed attack take @Damage[1d6[fire]] damage. If a q-metal morphoid causes creatures or objects to catch fire, water isn't an effective means to end the persistent damage from the chemical fire.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e.pf2e-battlezoo-su-effects.Item.UuVlQT9k7fhDswxw]{Effect: Flame Shroud}</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","s